# HTB Unified — Writeup

**Difficulty:** Easy
**Platform:** Hack The Box
**Category:** Linux / Web Exploitation / Privilege Escalation

## Executive Summary

Unified is an Easy-rated Linux machine centered around **UniFi Network Controller v6.4.54**, which ships a vulnerable version of Log4j and is susceptible to **Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228)**. Exploiting this flaw grants remote code execution as the `unifi` service user. From there, direct access to the application's local **MongoDB** instance allows an attacker to overwrite the administrator's password hash, log into the UniFi dashboard, and recover plaintext root SSH credentials stored in the application settings — leading to full root compromise.

**Technologies involved:**
- Apache Tomcat
- UniFi Network Controller
- Log4j (Log4Shell)
- MongoDB

**Attack chain:**

```
Nmap Enumeration
      │
      ▼
UniFi 6.4.54 Discovery
      │
      ▼
Research → Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228)
      │
      ▼
Remote Code Execution
      │
      ▼
Reverse Shell as unifi
      │
      ▼
MongoDB Enumeration
      │
      ▼
Replace Administrator Password Hash
      │
      ▼
Login to UniFi Dashboard
      │
      ▼
Recover Root SSH Credentials
      │
      ▼
SSH as root
```

